meta {
  name: Internal - Sync Employee Profile
  type: http
  seq: 90
}

post {
  url: {{hrServiceUrl}}/api/v1/internal/employees/sync
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Internal-Secret: {{internalServiceSecret}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "user_id": "{{userId}}",
    "tenant_id": "{{tenantId}}",
    "home_org_id": "{{orgId}}",
    "is_active": true,
    "date_of_joining": "2026-09-27",
    "actor_id": "{{secondUserId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Service-to-service only: identity-service calls this after Team create/edit.
  Hits hr-service DIRECTLY (not the gateway — the route is not proxied there).
  Set hrServiceUrl to hr-service's own origin, e.g. http://localhost:4007.

  Idempotent upsert of hr.employee_profiles. Returns data.outcome:
    created   — no profile existed; filed under home_org_id with date_of_joining
                (default today)
    updated   — org_id moved to home_org_id and/or is_active changed
    unchanged — already in step
    deleted   — HR soft-deleted this profile; it is not resurrected
  Joining date, code, department, designation and weekly off are never
  overwritten on an existing profile.

  400 when home_org_id is not a branch of tenant_id, or the user has no active
  mapping there. 401 without the correct X-Internal-Secret.
}
